# Git

A question is not permission. `reset`, `rebase`, `push --force`, `push --force-with-lease`, `branch -D`, `clean`, and `checkout -- <path>` run only on an order that names the operation and the target SHA or ref.

This holds for a conflict that another PR's merge caused: ask how to solve it (rebase and force-push, or merge `main` into the branch) before running either. In L7 the agent rebased the branch on `main` and reset another branch without an order after PR #136 merged; the owner then ordered the force pushes (PR #138).

When asked about such an operation, answer with the current `HEAD` SHA, the target SHA, what would disappear, and the exact command. Then wait.

- Finished work goes to a PR in the same turn, without waiting for an ask: commit on the Issue's branch, push it, and open the PR (`.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc`). The owner reviews on the PR, from wherever they are; uncommitted changes on this machine cannot be reviewed. Do not stop at "may I commit?".
- Long work runs in an agent worktree (`git worktree add .dev/<branch> <branch>`), not in the main working tree: the owner may switch that tree to another branch to review. In L2 the tree moved to `main` during the work; two edits landed there uncommitted, and the comparison apps were built from `main` (PR #125).
- This covers the Issue's own branch only. Never commit to `main` or push to it, and never merge.
- `git branch --show-current` is part of the command that commits. A chain that creates a branch can fail before it does, and the commit then lands on `main`.
- A push that follows a test is chained to it so that a failed test stops the push (`./build.ps1; if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { git push }`).
- When the gate fails only on a test that an open Issue tracks and the PR does not touch, the push still stops. The gate stops at the first failing step, so run the remaining test projects by hand; then write the failed test and its Issue under Verification and ask the owner whether to push. In PR #130 (only `docs/`) the gate failed on #126's message-loop test, the rest passed by hand, and the owner allowed the push.
- Read `gh pr view <n> --json state` before pushing to a branch that has a PR. A push to the branch of a merged PR recreates the deleted branch and reaches nothing.
- If history was rewritten, put the SHA from before the rewrite on the first line of the reply.
- Never skip hooks (`--no-verify`) or signing unless the owner orders it.
